# FoxDen — environment variable conventions
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values locally.
# `.env` is already gitignored — never commit real secrets.
#
# Expo only exposes variables prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ to client code
# (see https://docs.expo.dev/guides/environment-variables/). Anything
# without that prefix is server-side only (e.g. used by scripts/build.js
# or a future backend function) and is NEVER bundled into the app.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Existing — already used by app/foxscan.tsx and app/study-planner.tsx
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Domain the client calls for backend API routes (e.g. FoxScan, Study
# Planner). When unset, the app falls back to http://localhost:8080/api.
# Example: foxden-api.example.com (no protocol, no trailing slash)
EXPO_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Reserved for future backend work (Phase 1+) — not yet wired up.
# Left here so the convention is documented ahead of time; do not rely on
# these being read anywhere in the app yet.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase project URL and public anon key. Safe to expose to the client
# (protected by Supabase Row Level Security, not by secrecy).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Server-side only secrets for future backend functions (AI provider keys,
# Supabase service role key, etc.). These must NEVER use the EXPO_PUBLIC_
# prefix and must never be imported from client code under app/ or
# components/.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=